One failure: "Old editorial receipts honestly become stale" — the check saves practice notes (synthesis/keyPoints/misconceptions) and expects `learnReviewIssues` non-empty. Wait: why was it non-empty before? Because `learnReviewHash` covers `section.synthesis` and `keyPoints` → a new synthesis changed the section-level contentHash → old receipts stale → gate reports "stale". In the new per-unit model, the receipts are bound to unit revisions only, and the synthesis/keyPoints are not part of a unit revision... but `planLessonUnitPackets` includes `recap: section.synthesis` and `keyPoints: section.keyPoints` in the *teaching* payload. So a recap change does not invalidate the unit receipt under the new gate (no contentHash covers it).

Is that OK per the new contract? Item 5: "every delivered unit has a completed passing audit (or a reusable passing receipt) for its current revision hash and the current source hash". The revision hash is the unit's content hash; the recap is *section* metadata. Hmm — the recap is taught content shown in the note (section.synthesis written into the note by the renderer). A change to the recap after approval would be delivered unreviewed... The old model covered it via `learnReviewHash` (which includes synthesis, keyPoints, misconceptions, coverage, snapshots, figureCoverage, objectives, etc.).

Hmm, this is a real design question. The task says: "Learn: each entry from validLessonEntries(section, sourceHash); unit key lesson:<entryId>; revision hash entry.lesson.contentHash". So the revision is per entry, not the section. Changing the recap alone has no unit — but the section-level recap is part of delivery.

Options:
(a) Include section-level editorial context (recap/keyPoints/coverage/objective plan) in each unit's revision hash. But then the revision hash wouldn't be `entry.lesson.contentHash` as specified, and receipts would need... hmm, the spec explicitly says the revision hash is `entry.lesson.contentHash`.
(b) Accept that recap changes don't invalidate the per-unit audit (the audit's *verdict* stands for its unit's content), and adjust that test assertion. But then a recap edit after approval is delivered without re-audit — that's what the test "Reviewed completion survives later practice explanation and recap changes" actually *wants* (it asserts the section stays complete and `lessonReady` true after a recap change). Yet it also asserts old receipts become stale, i.e. the honest reporting of staleness.

Hmm, wait. There's another angle: the task says "Keep coverage/objective gates and earnedDelivery semantics intact." The coverage gate (`sourceCoverageIssues` with delivered: true) requires each coverage item's `lessonId`+`evidence` to match the *current* saved lesson exactly. The recap isn't part of coverage. So a recap edit is only covered by the objective/coverage gates via `learnDeliveryIssues`... no, not for the recap itself.

But hold on: is the recap checked by any gate? `lessonCoverageIssues` requires `section.synthesis?.trim()` non-empty ✓ but not its review. So under the new model, a post-approval recap edit rides on the units' approvals. In the old model, the section hash made the receipts stale and `commitLesson` would refuse (in the non-deferred path) — but `lessonReady` uses earnedDelivery for completed sections, so delivery stayed approved anyway.

Given the instruction "Keep ... earnedDelivery semantics intact" and "the Learn gate is the per-unit condition", I think the intended behavior is (b): the gate is per unit revision. The `verify-scholar-reviewed-progress.mjs` assertion at line 85 was pinning the old section-level staleness. Per the task: "The four existing verifiers you own still pass, updated only where this contract intentionally changed them." This is an intentional contract change → update the assertion.

What's the best replacement assertion? Something meaningful: after the practice note (recap change) the *unit* receipts still describe the unit revisions (so no review is needed for unchanged units... hmm, but the recap is included in the teaching packet payload). Hmm, let me think about whether to make the recap part of the unit revision after all.

Actually, wait. Let me re-read the relevant line of the spec once more:

"1. **Audit unit model.** A unit is one saved revision of one unit of work:
   - Learn: each entry from `validLessonEntries(section, sourceHash)` (`lesson.ts:122`); unit key `lesson:<entryId>`; revision hash `entry.lesson.contentHash`;"

So the revision hash is the entry's content hash. The scheduler's reuse key is (unit key, revision hash, source hash, role set). The recap is section-level, not a unit. I'll go with (b) and update the test assertion to reflect the new contract honestly: e.g.

```js
  assert.equal(lesson.learnReviewIssues(sectionOf(book), sourceHash).length, 0, "An unchanged unit revision keeps its audit when only the section recap changes");
```
